            "notes": "## Powers\n\nIn most rounds you want to start with [Face Tanking](item_f8af63d1-1fd4-4758-86ce-96f1ef7ea1ea) because this generates more cash, since the healing counts as cash. \n\nThe other option is [Focused Fusion](item_1123c91f-7348-4e50-aa1c-4a9961650f40), which I take if they have a less spammy comp or if they have flying heroes such as Mercy, Juno, Freja, or Pharah.\n\n## Items\n\nDVA benefits a lot from attack speed since she doesn\u2019t need to reload and she already shoots fast-firing, shotgun-like shots. That\u2019s why [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf), [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0), and [Power Playbook](item_6d8803cf-baa7-46ee-af91-51e7f2301418) provide the most damage you can get. With these items, you can already kill squishy targets in 2s or so.\n\nThen, against Zarya, you can run [Refraction Armor](item_dd020802-8d00-489d-93e0-930b80e31144) with [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0). Other beam damage isn\u2019t really relevant enough for you to pick, but the item is okay later when you have spare cash against Winston and Moira. I will not be going over this item again in the rounds ahead.",
