            "notes": "## Powers\n\nUsually I take [Focused Fusion](item_1123c91f-7348-4e50-aa1c-4a9961650f40) because this increases your damage at most distances and lets you play high grounds more effectively.\n\nIf the enemy team is very spammy with heroes like Cass, Soldier, Junkrat, Pharah, Freja, or Zen, then you should go with [Ultrawide Matrix](item_403fe162-4a59-4a8e-8af9-5f83267228e8) since you gain a lot of sustain and cash. It\u2019s also playable if you are dying a lot.\n\n## Items\n\n[Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f) provides about the highest damage you can get for cash.\n\n[Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) is very good as well and slightly cheaper. You need to run this if some enemies have armor already, since your damage gets cut in half otherwise on armor.\n\n[Multi-Task Mod](item_40997c0f-a8e3-46ba-b312-34c0790d0e87) has a very good effect and high damage. This is great v.s. heroes where you want to matrix what they do, like Cass right-click, Ana sleep dart/nade, or when you don\u2019t want them to heal off you, like a Reaper or Zen. It\u2019s a bit tricky to get used to, but keep in mind that you can shoot during Matrix.\n\nFor poorer rounds, grab [Icy Coolant](item_8b1c21e9-33e8-49a6-8277-a3a06d55a65f) or [Crusader Hydraulics](item_b64cee07-ca32-405d-987e-868b415bbc09) or [Wrist Wraps](item_19183386-c859-42ca-93f2-355d47d01e36).",
